    "body": "@jankatins I removed those for sake of consistency. You can either always use curlies or only where needed and here was the latter case so I simply followed the suit to make it easier for future maintainers.\n\nRegarding whether the extensive use of curlies is a best practice well, that's certainly a matter of personal preference but I'd argue it is not. Personally, I'm using them only for interpolations and stuff like length calculating, indexing, expansions otherwise I avoid them to minimize the clutter. I pretty much do what Mr. Shellharden _preaches_ https://github.com/anordal/shellharden/blob/master/how_to_do_things_safely_in_bash.md#should-i-use-curly-braces",
